 **THE RETRY's round costs at 8x8/1if** ([the round 3 ruling](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/894#issuecomment-6878014227), item 1). Round 2's measurement held 1,654 of THE RETRY's rounds in the `answering-every-port` arm over their stated cost (`round_grade.py`), every one a round of no notice beside 1, 2 or 4 refused attempts: up to 12,547, 19,326 and 23,343 cycles against 11,900, 15,300 and 22,100. A round's cold start, `AECP_ROUND_COLD_US` (`aecp_mbx.h`), was keyed on `MBX_N_IF`, so 8x8/1if took the 1x1's 85 us; a refused attempt's, `AECP_ATTEMPT_US` (`aecp.h`), was one 34 us at every shape. A stated cost under its measurement is the defect ([the round 2 ruling](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/894#issuecomment-6871343905), item (b)(ii)). Both are now stated for each shape in THE SHAPES (`CTRL_LOOP_RETRY_COLD_US`, `CTRL_LOOP_RETRY_ATTEMPT_US`, the table above), and the two AECP names are those names, never the interface count's.
 - **The measurement.** Round 2's rounds at 8x8/1if, the dearest at each count of refused attempts with notices charged at `AECP_NOTICE_US`: 2,206 cycles with none, 12,547 with one, 19,326 with two and 23,343 with four, every port. The rule is #665's definition of the attempt, what a round of `AECP_ROUND_PORTS` refusals costs past its cold start, a refusal, and of the cold start, what any round implies at it: the line that holds every round and a round of every port refused at its cost, and of those the one with the least cold start. It runs through the rounds of two and of four refused attempts, 15,309 cycles once and 2,008.5 a refused attempt (153.09 and 20.09 us); plus 5 %, rounded up to 5 us, 165 and 25 us. The other arms' rounds were within the earlier 85 + 34 k us, which lies under that line for every k up to the four ports. The 125 us round 2 reported was the cold start implied at the 34 us attempt; measuring the attempt too gives this line.
